seccomp, namespaces and the zygote are Linux's kernel.

M144 drew the line between being in the Linux FAMILY and having Linux's own
KERNEL, and //base, V8, //net and the display compositor have each met it
since. //content meets it in the place the distinction was invented for: the
sandbox.

A -k 0 build of //content failed in 86 places, and about thirty of them were
seccomp-bpf, the CLONE_NEW* namespaces, the setuid helper and the zygote.
None of that is a property of the Linux family; all of it is prctl(2),
seccomp(2), clone(2) and Linux's own system call numbers. Chromium already
has the flags that ask:

  use_seccomp_bpf          //sandbox/features.gni, was is_linux || ...
  compile_credentials      //sandbox/linux/BUILD.gn, declare_args
  compile_syscall_broker   //sandbox/linux/BUILD.gn, declare_args
  compile_suid_client      //sandbox/linux/BUILD.gn, declare_args
  use_zygote               //content/public/common/zygote/features.gni

and content/public/common/zygote/zygote_handle.h opens with

  #error "Can not use zygote without USE_ZYGOTE"

which is Chromium saying that a platform answering no is a configuration it
supports rather than an omission. The zygote is a fork server that clones
with CLONE_NEWPID and CLONE_NEWUSER so that a renderer starts from an address
space which has already paid for the shared libraries; what a platform
without one gets is what --no-zygote gets on a platform with one, and M149
already proved fork, exec and descriptor remapping work on this machine.

THE PRE-SANDBOX HOOKS

Five of them - the GPU process's, the audio service's, the speech
recognition service's, the screen AI service's and the network service's -
exist to open or dlopen what a service needs BEFORE seccomp-bpf forbids it.
Where there is no door there is nothing to do first.

AND TWO REFUSALS RATHER THAN RESULTS

sandbox::policy::Sandbox::IsProcessSandboxed() answers false here, and
RendererMainPlatformDelegate::EnableSandbox() returns false. Both are the
truthful answer and neither is a placeholder.

It is worth being exact about why this is not a gap. A process on this
machine IS confined: it carries a capability set assigned from a manifest at
spawn, and that set can only ever shrink. What is missing is not the
mechanism but the decision - nothing has yet been asked to spawn a renderer
with less authority than the browser - and a browser that answered yes on the
strength of a set nobody reduced would be making a claim nothing can check.
IsProcessSandboxed is what about:sandbox reports and what several DCHECKs
believe. That is M65's rule.

The condition for changing both is nameable: the launcher spawning a renderer
with strictly less authority than itself, and these functions being able to
ask what this process was given.

inotify(7) comes with them, in content/browser/BUILD.gn: content already
ships file_path_watcher_stub.cc for a platform without a file watcher, and
this keeps it rather than replacing it with the inotify one.

